---
// "Worth the visit?" — a vote, and beside it a separate way to report a problem.
//
// Split apart 2026-08-16 on Hidde's instruction: "je kunt een boom niet leuk
// vinden of niet de moeite vinden zonder dat er iets mis is." The first version
// (his own design of 2026-08-14) hung four chips off the thumbs-down under the
// heading "What was wrong?", and one of those chips was "Not that special",
// which is an opinion rather than a fault. So the control asked everyone who
// simply was not impressed to file a fault report, and gave everyone who loved
// the tree but found the pin wrong no way in at all.
//
// The convention, checked against the standing references before rebuilding:
// Google Maps keeps its rating and its "Suggest an edit" as two separate entry
// points; AllTrails separates the star rating from reporting conditions;
// YouTube and Reddit separate the vote from Report. Everywhere, opinion and
// error report are siblings, never nested. Nesting hides the report from the
// people most likely to have one and interrogates the people least likely.
//
// So: thumbs are a pure vote, one tap, no follow-up. "Something's wrong" is its
// own button that opens the fact chips, and "Not that special" is gone, because
// the thumbs-down already says it. The two are independent: someone may vote up
// and still report a wrong pin.
//
// Where a report goes is unchanged: the same Supabase submissions table the
// /contribute form uses (kind 'feedback'), where Step 0b picks it up, and a
// dead or wrong-location report gets checked the same day.
//
// Votes are stored from day one and shown to nobody: at current volume a count
// would be fake authority, and re-ranking waits until the numbers are honest
// (DECISIONS.md 2026-08-14). One vote per tree per browser via localStorage,
// the passport pattern; the report carries its own separate key so a vote never
// blocks a correction.
interface Props {
  treeId: string;
  city: string;
  treeName: string;
  compact?: boolean;
}
const { treeId, city, treeName, compact = false } = Astro.props;
const formLink = `/contribute?kind=correction&city=${encodeURIComponent(city)}&tree=${encodeURIComponent(treeName)}`;
---
<div class={`worthit${compact ? " worthit-compact" : ""}`} data-tree={treeId} data-city={city} data-name={treeName}>
  <div class="worthit-row">
    <span class="worthit-q">Been here? Worth the visit?</span>
    <button type="button" class="worthit-btn" data-vote="up" aria-label={`Yes, ${treeName} was worth the visit`}>👍</button>
    <button type="button" class="worthit-btn" data-vote="down" aria-label={`No, ${treeName} was not worth the visit`}>👎</button>
    <span class="worthit-done" hidden>Thanks, counted. Tap again to undo.</span>
    <button type="button" class="worthit-report" aria-expanded="false">Something's wrong</button>
  </div>
  <div class="worthit-why" hidden>
    <span class="worthit-q">What's wrong?</span>
    <button type="button" class="worthit-chip" data-reason="dead or gone">It's dead or gone</button>
    <button type="button" class="worthit-chip" data-reason="wrong location">Wrong location</button>
    <button type="button" class="worthit-chip" data-reason="could not reach it">Couldn't reach it</button>
    <a class="worthit-chip worthit-chip-link" href={formLink}>Something else</a>
  </div>
  <span class="worthit-thanks" hidden>Thanks, we'll check it.</span>
  <a class="worthit-more" href={formLink} hidden>Add a detail (optional)</a>
</div>
